ts, the midi-unpitched element specifies a MIDI 1.0 note","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"number ranging from 1 to 128. It is usually used with MIDI banks for percussion.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Note that MIDI 1.0 note numbers are generally specified from 0 to 127 rather than","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the 1 to 128 numbering used in this element.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"midiUnpitched"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The volume element value is a percentage of the maximum ranging from 0 to 100, with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"decimal values allowed. This corresponds to a scaling value for the MIDI 1.0 channel","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"volume controller.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"volume"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The pan and elevation elements allow placing of sound in a 3-D space relative to the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"listener. Both are expressed in degrees ranging from -180 to 180. For pan, 0 is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"straight ahead, -90 is hard left, 90 is hard right, and -180 and 180 are directly","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"behind the listener.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"pan"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The elevation and pan elements allow placing of sound in a 3-D space relative to the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"listener. Both are expressed in degrees ranging from -180 to 180. For elevation, 0","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is level with the listener, 90 is directly above, and -90 is directly below.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"elevation"}]}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Initializer","symbolKind":"init","title":"init(id:midiChannel:midiName:midiBank:midiProgram:midiUnpitched:volume:pan:elevation:)","externalI